    <summary>Prepare repositories for AI-assisted development with the AgentRC CLI.</summary>
    <description>
## AgentRC

AgentRC is an experimental context-engineering CLI for AI coding agents. It evaluates a repository's AI-readiness and generates tailored instruction files, evaluations, and development configurations.

This package installs the `@microsoft/agentrc` npm package globally in the npm prefix of the user running Chocolatey. It requires Node.js 22+ (provided by the `nodejs-lts` dependency). Some AgentRC workflows also require GitHub Copilot CLI and GitHub or Azure DevOps authentication. The upstream project is experimental and may introduce breaking changes.

### Package details

If you already have Node.js 22+ installed, you can skip the `nodejs-lts` dependency by using `--ignore-dependencies`
    </description><releaseNotes><![CDATA[https://www.npmjs.com/package/@microsoft/agentrc/v/2.0.1-103]]></releaseNotes>
    
    <dependencies>
      <dependency id="nodejs-lts" />
